#: ../../troubleshooting/Variables_Examples.rst:4
msgid "Variables"
msgstr "Variables"

#: ../../troubleshooting/Variables_Examples.rst:6
msgid ""
"A vast number of variables are available for use in Tasks, Scripts, "
"Templates, Resource Names, Cloud-Init User Data and Option List configs."
msgstr ""
"Una gran cantidad de variables están disponibles para usar en Tareas, "
"Scripts, Plantillas, Nombres de Recursos, Datos de Usuario de Cloud-Init y "
"configuraciones de Listas de Opciones."

#: ../../troubleshooting/Variables_Examples.rst:8
msgid "Variables are case sensitive"
msgstr "Las variables distinguen entre mayúsculas y minúsculas"

#: ../../troubleshooting/Variables_Examples.rst:11
msgid "Pre-Provision Vars"
msgstr "Variables de pre-aprovisionamiento"

#: ../../troubleshooting/Variables_Examples.rst:13
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A subset of variables are available for Instance, Host Name and "
"Hostnames. These can be passed inside ``${ }`` blocks during provisioning"
" or in relevant policy configs. Groovy syntax can be resolved to allow "
"for dynamic name generation as shown in some of the examples below."
msgstr ""
"A subset of variables están disponibles for Instance, Host Name and "
"Hostnames. These puede ser passed inside ``${ }`` blocks during "
"provisioning or in relevant policy configs. Groovy syntax puede ser "
"resolved to allow for dynamic name generation as shown in some of the "
"examples below."

#: ../../troubleshooting/Variables_Examples.rst:15
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Instance Naming Policy example: ``${userInitials}-${cloudCode}-${platform"
" == 'windows' ? 'W' : 'L'}-${sequence}``"
msgstr ""
"Ejemplo de Política de Nombres de Instancia: "
"``${userInitials}-${cloudCode}-${platform == 'windows' ? 'W' : "
"'L'}-${sequence}``"

#: ../../troubleshooting/Variables_Examples.rst:17
msgid "Available variables for Naming Policy naming patterns include:"
msgstr "Las variables disponibles para los patrones de nomenclatura de las Políticas de Nombres incluyen:"

#: ../../troubleshooting/Variables_Examples.rst:19
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"${account}\n"
"${accountId}\n"
"${accountName}\n"
"${accountNumber}\n"
"${accountType}\n"
"${cloudCode}\n"
"${cloudName}\n"
"${customerNumber}\n"
"${customOptions.fieldName}\n"
"${groupCode}\n"
"${groupName}\n"
"${instance.instanceContext} # Environment Code\n"
"${platform == 'windows' ? 'w':'l'} # results in `w` for Windows platforms"
" and `l` for Linux Platforms\n"
"${platform}\n"
"${provisionType}\n"
"${sequence} # results in 1\n"
"${sequence+100} # results in 101\n"
"${sequence.toString().padLeft(5,'0')} # results in 00001\n"
"${tenantId}\n"
"${tenant} # Tenant Name\n"
"${tenantSubdomain}\n"
"${type}\n"
"${userId}\n"
"${userInitials}\n"
"${username}"
msgstr ""
"${account}\n${accountId}\n${accountName}\n${accountNumber}\n${accountType}\"
"n${cloudCode}\n${cloudName}\n${customerNumber}\n${customOptions.fieldName}\"
"n${groupCode}\n${groupName}\n${instance.instanceContext} # Environment "
"Code\n${platform == 'windows' ? 'w':'l'} # results in `w` for Windows "
"platforms and `l` for Linux "
"Platforms\n${platform}\n${provisionType}\n${sequence} # results in "
"1\n${sequence+100} # results in 101\n${sequence.toString().padLeft(5,'0')} "
"# results in 00001\n${tenantId}\n${tenant} # Tenant "
"Name\n${tenantSubdomain}\n${type}\n${userId}\n${userInitials}\n${username}"

#: ../../troubleshooting/Variables_Examples.rst:47
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"An example Instance Name Policy using a naming pattern with User "
"Initials, Cloud Code, Instance Type, and a sequential number starting at "
"3000 is ``${userInitials}-${cloudCode}-${type}-${sequence+3000}``, "
"resulting in an Instance Name of **md-vmwd3-centos-3001** for the first "
"instance, followed by **md-vmwd3-centos-3002** and so on."
msgstr ""
"An example Instancia Name Policy using a naming pattern with Usuario "
"Initials, Cloud Code, Instancia Type, and a sequential number starting at "
"3000 is ``${userInitials}-${cloudCode}-${tipo}-${sequence+3000}``, "
"resulting in an Instancia Name of **md-vmwd3-centos-3001** for the first "
"instancia, followed by **md-vmwd3-centos-3002** and so on."

#: ../../troubleshooting/Variables_Examples.rst:49
msgid ""
"It's not recommended that users include \">\", \"<\", \"%\", \"$\", or "
"\"=\" in naming policies."
msgstr ""
"No se recomienda que los usuarios incluyan \">\", \"<\", \"%\", \"$\" o "
"\"=\" en las políticas de nombres."

